{
  "title": "Aamaal of the Day of Arafah (9th Zilhajj)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "The devotional acts on this day are as follows:\nFirst: It is recommended to perform bathing on this day.\nSecond: It is recommended to visit the holy tomb of Imam Husayn (a.s.), for its reward is equal to the reward of one thousand times of Hajj, one thousand times of Umrah, and one thousand times of jihad (holy war), and even more. The narrations entailing the great merits and rewards of visiting the holy tomb of Imam Husayn (a.s.) on the ninth of Zilhajj have been uninterruptedly reported. If fact, the reward of visiting the holy tomb of Imam Husayn (a.s.) and having the honor of attending therein is not less than the reward of attending on Mount Arafah and even more.\nThe form of Ziyarah on this day will be cited in the section of Ziyarat.\nThird: It is recommended to offer a two unit prayer immediately after the obligatory Asr Prayer before saying the supplicatory prayers of Arafah. This prayer should be offered outdoors and it should include confessions of sins. One who offers this prayer will be granted the reward of attending on Mount Arafah and having all sins forgiven.\nAfter this prayer, it is recommended to begin with the acts and supplications of the Arafah Day that are reported from the Holy Infallibles (a.s.). Although these acts and supplications are too numerous to be mentioned here. Some of them are:\nIn al-Misbah, al-Kaf’ami says that it is recommended to observe fasting on the Arafah Day, unless fasting prevents from saying the supplications. It is also recommended to bathe oneself before midday (zohr) and to visit the holy tomb of Imam Husayn (a.s.) on day and night. At midday (zohr), it is recommended to leave one’s house and offer the obligatory Zohr and Asr prayers outdoors with complete performance of their parts. After accomplishment, it is recommended to offer a two unit prayer reciting Surah al-Faatehah and Surah al-Tawheed in the first unit and Surah al-Faatehah and Surah al-Kaferun in the second. After that, it is recommended to offer a four unit prayer reciting at each unit Surah al-Faatehah once and repeating Surah al-Tawheed fifty times.\nThis is in fact the prayer of Imam Ali Ameer al-Momineen (a.s.) that has been already mentioned within the rites of Fridays.\nIn Iqbal al-Aamaal, Sayyid Ibn Taaoos says:\nSay the following doxology (zikr) that is reported from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.):\nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ فِی السَّمَآءِ عَرْشُہٗ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE FIS SAMAAA-E A’RSHOHU\nGlory be to the One Whose Throne is in the heaven; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ فِی الْاَرْضِ حُکْمُہٗ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE FIL ARZE HUKMOHU \nGlory be to the One Whose authority is in the earth; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ فِیْ الْقُبُوْرِ قَضَاوُہٗ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE FIL QOBOORE QAZAA-OHU \nGlory be to the One Whose decree is in the graves; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ فِی الْبَحْرِ سَبِیْلُہٗ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE FIL BAHRE SABEELOHU \nGlory be to the One Whose path is in the sea; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ فِی النَّارِ سُلْطَانُہٗ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE FIN NAARE SULTAANOHU \nGlory be to the One Whose dominion is in the Fire; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ فِی الْجَنَّۃِ رَحْمَتُہٗ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE FIL JANNATE RAHMATOHU \nGlory be to the One Whose mercy is in Paradise; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ فِی الْقِیَامَۃِ عَدْلُہٗ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE FIL QEYAAMATE A’DLOHU \nGlory be to the One Whose justice is in the Resurrection; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ رَفَعَ السَّمَآءَ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE RAFA-A’S SAMAAA-A \nGlory be to the One Who raised the heaven; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ بَسَطَ الْاَرْضَ \nSUBHAANAL LAZEE BASATAL ARZA \nGlory be to the One Who spread the earth; \nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ مَلْجَاَ وَ لَامَنْجَا مِنْهُ اِلَّا اِلَیْهِ.\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE MALJA-A WA LAA MANJAA MINHO ILLAA ELAYHE.\nGlory be to the One from Whom there is no shelter nor escape except toward Him.\nThen, repeat the following doxology (zikr) one hundred times:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHE WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE \nGlory be to Allah, and all praise is due to Allah, \nوَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَ اللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ.\nWA LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAL LAAHO AKBARO.\nand there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.\nThen, repeat Surah al-Tawheed one hundred times, Ayah al-Kursi one hundred times, and invoke blessings upon Muhammad and his Household one hundred times.\nThen say 100 times:\nلَا اِلٰہَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَحْدَہٗ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَہٗ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU \nThere is no god but Allah, alone without partner; \nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَ لَهُ الْحَمْدُ یُحْیِیْ وَ یُمِیْتُ \nLAHUL MULKO WA LAHUL HAMDO YOHYEE WA YOMEETO \nto Him belongs the kingdom and to Him belongs the praise; He gives life and He causes death, \nوَ یُمِیْتُ وَ یُحْیِیْ وَ هُوَ حَیٌّ لَا یَمُوْتُ \nWA YOMEETO WA YOHYEE WA HOWA HAYYUN LAA YAMOOTO \nand He causes death and He gives life; and He is the Ever-Living who does not die; \nبِیَدِهِ الْخَیْرُ وَ هُوْ عَلٰی کُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ.\nBEYADEHIL KHAYRO WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAYIN QADEER.\nin His hand is all good, and He has power over all things.\nThen, repeat the following doxological and supplicatory statements ten times each:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُاللهَ الَّذِیْ لَا اِلٰہَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْحَیُّ الْقَیُّوْمُ وَ اَتُوْبُ اِلَیْهِ.\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHAL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWAL HAYYUL QAYYOOMO WA ATOOBO ELAYHE.\nI seek forgiveness from Allah, there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer, and I turn to Him in repentance.\nيَا اَللهُ\nYAA ALLAAHO\nO Allah\nيَا رَحْمٰنُ\nYAA RAHMAANO\nO All-Beneficent\nيَا رَحِيْمُ\nYAA RAHEEMO\nO All-Merciful\nيَا بَدِيْعَ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ\nYAA BADEE-A’S SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ\nO Originator of the heavens and the earth\nیَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAM\nO Lord of Majesty and Honor\nيَا حَيُّ يَا قَيُّوْمُ\nYAA HAYYO YAA QAYYOOM\nO Ever-Living, O Sustainer\nيَا حَنَّانُ يَا مَنَّانُ\nYAA HANNAANO YAA MANNAAN\nO All-Affectionate, O Bestower of Favors\nيَا لَا اِلٰہَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nYAA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANT\nO You besides Whom there is no god\nاٰمِيْنَ.\nAAMEEN.\nAmen.\nThen, say the following:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ یَا مَنْ هُوَ اَقْرَبُ اِلَیَّ مِنْ حَبْلِ الْوَرِیْدِ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA YAA MAN HOWA AQRABO ELAYYA MIN HABLIL WAREEDE \nO Allah, I ask You, O He who is closer to me than my jugular vein; \nیَا مَنْ یَحُوْلُ بَیْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَ قَلْبِہٖ \nYAA MAN YAHOOLO BAYNAL MAR-E WA QALBEHI \nO He who comes between a man and his heart; \nیَا مَنْ هُوْ بِالْمَنْظَرِ الْاَعْلَی وَ بِالْاُفُقِ الْمُبِیْنِ \nYAA MAN HOWA BIL-MANZARIL A-A’LAA WA BIL-OFOQIL MOBEENE \nO He who is in the highest vantage point and at the clear horizon; \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ الرَّحْمٰنُ عَلَی الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوٰی \nYAA MAN HOWAR RAHMAANO A’LAL A’RSHIS TAWAA \nO He who is the All-Beneficent, established upon the Throne; \nیَا مَنْ لَیْسَ كَمِثْلِہٖ شَیْءٌ وَ هُوَ السَّمِیْعُ الْبَصِیْرُ \nYAA MAN LAYSA KAMISLEHI SHAY-UN WA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L BASEER \nO He whom nothing is like, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing; \nاَسْئَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّیَ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَّآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ.\nAS-ALOKA AN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN.\nI ask You to bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.\nThe, submit your needs and they will be granted, by the permission of Almighty Allah.\nYou may then say the following supplicatory prayer that is reported from Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) who said: If you wish to please Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad - peace be upon them all - you may say the following invocation:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ یَا اَجْوَدَ مَنْ اَعْطٰی \nALLAAHUMMA YAA AJWADA MAN A-A’TAA \nO Allah, O most Generous of those who give, \nوَ یَا خَیْرَ مَنْ سُئِلَ \nWA YAA KHAYRA MAN SO-ELA \nO Best of those who are asked, \nوَ یَا اَرْحَمَ مَنِ اسْتُرْحِمَ \nWA YAA ARHAMA MANIS TURHEMA \nand O most Merciful of those from whom mercy is sought. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِہٖ فِی الْاَوَّلِیْنَ \nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALEHI FIL AWWALEENA \nO Allah, bless Muhammad and his family among the first generations, \nوَ صَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِہٖ فِی الْآخِرِیْنَ \nWA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALEHI FIL AAKHEREENA \nand bless Muhammad and his family among the latter generations, \nوَ صَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِہٖ فِی الْمَلَاءِ الْاَعلٰی \nWA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALEHI FIL MALAA-IL A-A’LAA \nand bless Muhammad and his family in the highest assembly, \nوَ صَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِہٖ فِی الْمُرْسَلِیْنَ \nWA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALEHI FIL MURSALEENA \nand bless Muhammad and his family among the messengers. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا وَآلِهِ الْوَسِیْلَۃَ الْفَضِیْلَۃَ \nALLAAHUMMA A-A’TE MOHAMMADAN WA AALEHIL WASEELATAL FAZEELATA \nO Allah, grant Muhammad and his family the right of mediation, the excellence, \nوَ الشَّرَفَ وَ الرِّفْعَۃَ وَ الدَّرَجَۃَ الْكَبِیْرَۃَ \nWASH SHARAFA WAR RIF-A’TA WAD DARAJATAL KABEERATA \nthe honor, the eminence, and the great station. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّی اٰمَنْتُ بِمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ آلِہٖ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AAMANTO BE-MOHAMMADIN SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \nO Allah, I have believed in Muhammad—blessings of Allah be upon him and his family—\nوَ لَمْ اَرَہٗ فَلَا تَحْرِمْنِیْ فِی الْقِیَامَۃِ رُؤْیَتَہٗ \nWA LAM ARAHU FALAA TAHRIMNEE FIL QEYAAMATE ROAYATAHU \nthough I have not seen him, so do not deprive me of his vision on the Day of Resurrection; \nوَ ارْزُقْنِیْ صُحْبَتَہٗ وَ تَوَفَّنِیْ عَلٰی مِلَّتِہٖ \nWAR ZUQNEE SOHBATAHU WA TAWAFFANEE A’LAA MILLATEHI \ngrant me his companionship, cause me to die upon his creed, \nوَ اسْقِنِیْ مِنْ حَوْضِہٖ مَشْرَبًا \nWAS QENEE MIN HAWZEHI MASHRABAN \nand give me to drink from his fountain a drink \nرَوِیًّا سَآئِغًا هَنِیْٓئًا لَا اَظْمَاُ بَعْدَہٗ اَبَدًا \nRAWIYYAN SAAA-EGHAN HANEE-AN LAA AZMA-O BA’DAHU ABADAN \nthat is quenching, easy to swallow, and pleasant, after which I shall never thirst again. \nاِنَّكَ عَلٰی کُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ \nINNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER \nIndeed, You have power over all things. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّی اٰمَنْتُ بِمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّی اَللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَآلِہٖ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AAMANTO BE-MOHAMMADIN SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \nO Allah, I have believed in Muhammad—blessings of Allah be upon him and his family—\nوَ لَمْ اَرَہٗ فَعَرِّفْنِیْ فِی الْجِنَانِ وَجْهَہٗ \nWA LAM ARAHO FA-A’RRIFNEE FIL JENAANE WAJHAHU \nthough I have not seen him, so make his face known to me in the gardens of Paradise. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ بَلِّغْ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّی اَللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ آلِہٖ \nALLAAHUMMA BALLIGH MOHAMMADAN SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \nO Allah, convey to Muhammad—blessings of Allah be upon him and his family—\nمِنِّیْ تَحِیَّۃً كَثِیْرَۃً وَ سَلَامًا.\nMINNEE TAHIYYATAN KASEERATAN WA SALAAMAA.\nabundant greetings and peace from me.\nYou may then say the famous supplicatory prayer known as Dua Umm-e-Dawood, which has been previously cited within the devotional acts of Rajab.\nYou may then say the following doxology (zikr) whose reward is too much to be mentioned:\nسُبْحَانَ اللهِ قَبْلَ کُلِّ اَحَدٍ \nSUBHAANAL LAAHE QABLA KULLE AHADIN \nGlory be to Allah before everyone, \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَعْدَ کُلِّ اَحَدٍ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE BA’DA KULLE AHADIN \nand Glory be to Allah after everyone, \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مَعَ کُلِّ اَحَدٍ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE MA-A’ KULLE AHADIN \nand Glory be to Allah with everyone. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ یَبْقٰی رَبُّنَا وَ یَفْنٰی کُلُّ اَحَدٍ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE YABQAA RABBONAA WA YAFNAA KULLO AHADIN \nGlory be to Allah; our Lord remains while everyone perishes. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ تَسْبِیْحًا یَفْضُلُ تَسْبِیْحَ الْمُسَبِّحِیْنَ فَضْلًا كَثِیْرًا قَبْلَ کُلِّ اَحَدٍ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE TASBEEHAN YAFZOLO TASBEEHAL MOSABBEHEENA FAZLAN KASEERAN QABLA KULLE AHADIN \nGlory be to Allah with a glorification that excels the glorification of those who glorify Him by a great excellence before everyone. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ تَسْبِیْحًا یَفْضُلُ تَسْبِیْحَ الْمُسَبِّحِیْنَ فَضْلًا كَثِیْرًا بَعْدَ کُلِّ اَحَدٍ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE TASBEEHAN YAFZOLO TASBEEHAL MOSABBEHEENA FAZLAN KASEERAN BA’DA KULLE AHADIN \nGlory be to Allah with a glorification that excels the glorification of those who glorify Him by a great excellence after everyone. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ تَسْبِیْحًا یَفْضُلُ تَسْبِیْحَ الْمُسَبِّحِیْنَ فَضْلًا كَثِیْرًا مَعَ کُلِّ اَحَدٍ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE TASBEEHAN YAFZOLO TASBEEHAL MOSABBEHEENA FAZLAN KASEERAN MA-A’ KULLE AHADIN \nGlory be to Allah with a glorification that excels the glorification of those who glorify Him by a great excellence with everyone. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ تَسْبِیْحًا یَفْضُلُ تَسْبِیْحَ الْمُسَبِّحِیْنَ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE TASBEEHAN YAFZOLO TASBEEHAL MOSABBEHEENA \nGlory be to Allah with a glorification that excels the glorification of those who glorify Him \nفَضْلًا كَثِیْرًا لِرَبِّنَا الْبَاقِیْ وَ یَفْنٰی کُلُّ اَحَدٍ \nFAZLAN KASEERAN LE-RABBENAL BAAQEE WA YAFNAA KULLO AHADIN \nby a great excellence for our Lord who remains while everyone perishes. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ تَسْبِیْحًا لَا یُحْصٰی وَ لَا یُدْرٰی \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE TASBEEHAN LAA YOHSAA WA LAA YUDRAA \nGlory be to Allah with a glorification that cannot be numbered, nor perceived, \nوَ لَا یُنْسٰی وَ لَا یَبْلٰی وَ لَا یَفْنٰی وَ لَیْسَ لَہٗ مُنْتَہٰی \nWA LAA YUNSAA WA LAA YABLAA WA LAA YAFNAA WA LAYSA LAHU MUNTAHAA \nnor forgotten, nor worn out, nor exhausted, and for which there is no end. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ تَسْبِیْحًا یَدُوْمُ بِدَوَامِہٖ \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE TASBEEHAN YADOOMO BE-DAWAAMEHI \nGlory be to Allah with a glorification that lasts with His everlastingness \nوَ یَبْقٰی بِبَقَآئِہٖ فِیْ سِنِی الْعَالَمِیْنَ \nWA YABQAA BE-BAQAAA-EHI FEE SENIL A’ALAMEENA \nand remains with His subsistence throughout the years of the worlds, \nوَ شُهُوْرِ الدُّهُوْرِ وَ اَیَّامِ الدُّنْیَا وَ سَاعَاتِ اللَّیْلِ وَالنَّہَارِ. \nWA SHOHOORID DOHOORE WA AYYAAMID DUNYAA WA SAA-A’ATIL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE. \nthe months of the ages, the days of the world, and the hours of the night and the day. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللهِ اَبَدَا الْاَبَدِ وَ مَعَ الْاَبَدِ